        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Text of True Purpose: &quot;<span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(37, 37, 37); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">Select a non-Hero Target. Until the start of your next turn, all Bounty cards also affect that target and are not destroyed when a target leaves play.&quot;</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(37, 37, 37); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">This says that &quot;All Bounty cards are not destroyed when a target leaves play.&quot; &nbsp;This says to me that Whole Gang would not have been destroyed when Old Lady was. &nbsp;The key word is &quot;a target&quot; as opposed to &quot;the target&quot;. &nbsp;If it was &quot;the target&quot; then that would indicate that the destruction prevention was tied to the target mentioned earlier, but since it is &quot;a target&quot;, I&#39;d apply the protection to the original as well.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(37, 37, 37); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">As far as stacking goes, I don&#39;t think that you can stack a bounty by pointing it at the target it&#39;s already attached to, but I&#39;m less confident about my reasoning there.</span></p>",
